        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified, but event-level evidence is unavailable\n\nThe relevant order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order ID **WO-2025-09-004**, for **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine–Dekoven operation.\n\n| Requested item | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Source transaction ID | Cannot be determined from the available records |\n| Event amount | Cannot be determined |\n| Exact event-created time | Cannot be determined |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot be calculated without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Whether that status is consistent with Oracle policy | Cannot be concluded without the event record |\n\nThe source timestamp has **no timezone or UTC offset**, so none has been inferred.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe readable records contain the work order and cost period, but **no cost-event rows**. The supporting event input repeatedly returned **404: “Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”** I escalated the missing input and checked the available alternate evidence, but could not obtain the required event details.\n\nConsequently, I **cannot establish whether an event was created after Pending Close**. Missing records must not be interpreted as evidence that no late event occurred.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” printed page 225 / PDF page 233**, states that:\n\n- New transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period **are not staged** in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting; they are processed after the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered **before** Pending Close continue processing, including those in an error state.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments** continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nThus, an ordinary manufacturing cost transaction newly created after **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** should be held rather than processed while the period remains Pending Close. Applying that rule to this event requires its missing type, creation timestamp, and recorded accounting status.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_2ef356752d28/audit-report.json`; the submitted review is marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
